<!--
  Sparkle appcast for the Air Control Mac helper.

  PLACEHOLDER — no releases have shipped yet, so this feed is deliberately empty
  (a feed with zero <item> elements is valid and simply tells Sparkle "you are up
  to date"). Sparkle is deferred until M8; see docs/00-decisions.md Addendum D5.

  This file is served verbatim from the landing page's GitHub Pages site at
  /appcast.xml. Next.js copies everything under site/public/ into site/out/
  untouched, so nothing here is parsed, rewritten or routed by the site build.

  When releases begin, the release workflow should replace this file (or write to
  it) with entries of the form:

    <item>
      <title>1.0.0</title>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>100</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<ul><li>What changed.</li></ul>]]></description>
      <enclosure
        url="https://github.com/devashish2531/air-control/releases/download/v1.0.0/AirControl-1.0.0.dmg"
        length="0"
        type="application/octet-stream"
        sparkle:edSignature="..." />
    </item>

  The EdDSA signature is produced by Sparkle's `sign_update` tool with the
  project's private key; the matching public key lives in the app's Info.plist as
  SUPublicEDKey. Never publish an item without a signature.
-->
